<!--
    android_manifest_additions.xml
    ================================
    This block must be merged inside the <application> tag of the final
    AndroidManifest.xml generated by python-for-android.

    How to use it with buildozer (recommended approach):
    -------------------------------------------------
    buildozer/python-for-android don't offer a fully declarative way to
    merge manifest blocks like this. The simplest reliable way currently
    available:

    1) The recommended path is the p4a hook via the included
       buildozer_hooks.py file (see buildozer.spec: p4a.hook), which
       automatically injects this block into AndroidManifest.xml after
       generation.

    2) Manual alternative (if you exported the project as an Android
       Studio project from p4a): open AndroidManifest.xml and paste the
       following inside <application ...> ... </application>
-->
<provider
    android:name="androidx.core.content.FileProvider"
    android:authorities="${applicationId}.fileprovider"
    android:exported="false"
    android:grantUriPermissions="true">
    <meta-data
        android:name="android.support.FILE_PROVIDER_PATHS"
        android:resource="@xml/file_paths" />
</provider>

<!--
    Notes for Android 13+ (API 33/34):
    - No need to add <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAMERA"/>
      here manually; buildozer.spec adds it via android.permissions = CAMERA.
    - Never add WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE or READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE; saving is
      done exclusively via Storage Access Framework (ACTION_CREATE_DOCUMENT),
      which needs no permission at all.
    - If you later add a "pick a photo from the gallery" feature, you will
      only need:
          <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.READ_MEDIA_IMAGES"/>
      (the new Android 13 permission that replaces READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE).
    - targetSdkVersion 33/34 enforces explicit FLAG_GRANT_READ_URI_PERMISSION
      when sharing (already applied in utils/share_utils.py).
-->
